index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bbc956eb7903389626ef58ae0bae935b0cf1784b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ms58-dominance-profile.md
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# Experimental dominance and correction profiling
+
+This diagnostic derivative starts from selected correction-on Kayros `9d64b7c53ddaea7a578d247ebd28db43ae0d4e56`. We measure the selected source independently from the older correction-off extension profile. We introduce no dominance optimization, caching, filter approximation, PWL arithmetic change, or solver experiment.
+
+The CMake option `KAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILING` defaults to `OFF`. All instrumentation is preprocessor guarded. OFF preprocessing has identical C++ tokens to selected9d for the 3 modified translation units and the 3 modified class headers. The CMake definition is public on `lera`, so the `_lera` bridge and its library share class layouts. The independent `_core` and its ILS code receive no profiling definition. Production and performance builds must keep this option disabled.
+
+## Activation and records
+
+Build a separate CPLEX diagnostic variant with `-DKAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILING=ON`. Set `KAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILE` to a new JSONL path before creating the solver. The owner exclusively creates this file with `fopen(..., "wx")`. An existing file causes an error without being overwritten. Missing or empty runtime opt-in leaves profiling inactive. A compiled diagnostic variant still has instrumentation overhead when runtime profiling is inactive and is unsuitable as a performance control.
+
+The optional variables `KAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILE_STRIDE` and `KAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILE_OFFSET` default to `1009` and `0`. Invalid integers, a zero stride, or an offset at least equal to the stride fail before opening the file. We sample zero-based whole calls whose ordinal modulo stride equals offset, separately for dominance, correction and merge maintenance, separately for each direction, resetting at every pricing call.
+
+A flushed `profile_open` identifies schema `kayros-ms58-dominance-profile-v1`, exact selected base, sampling rule and clock. Each pricing call writes a flushed `pricing_begin` with the pricing problem, level and effective flags, including correcting, partial dominance, cost and elementarity relaxation, each direction's NG setting, sorting, extension mode, arithmetic mode and limits. Cumulative `pricing_progress` is checked after sampled calls and monodirectional batches, with a minimum interval of 5 seconds. A long call or merge can delay a progress record.
+
+Normal pricing return writes `pricing_end`, `pricing_returned=true`, the unchanged native log, explicit `native_status`, returned-route count and pool size. Native statuses retain their distinction between Finished, TimeLimitReached, MemoryLimitReached and SolutionLimitReached. A return record does not assert solver closure or proof validity. An unmatched begin remains unfinished after exceptions or termination. Destructors do not finish pricing or interrupted episodes. Counters from finished episodes are committed at explicit normal returns. Attempts and sampled attempts can therefore exceed finished counts in an interrupted call.
+
+All state belongs to one `BidirectionalLabeling` instance. Its monodirectional helpers receive stable direction pointers. A PWL scratch helper receives an optional accumulator scoped to its enclosing dominance or correction call. No mutable global or thread-local profiling state is added.
+
+## Attribution and counters
+
+Each operation groups counters and sampled times by its final outcome. For dominance, `eliminated` means the candidate was fully eliminated. For correction, it means the call retired at least 1 stored label. For merge maintenance, it means at least 1 empty label was removed from the merge index. The `survived` correction group includes calls that changed domains or costs while retiring no label, as well as the existing cost-relaxation shortcut. No-return episodes are excluded from either outcome group.
+
+Each sample measures whole-call steady-clock wall time and partitions it exactly into construction, scan and materialization nanoseconds. Construction covers PWL scratch creation. Materialization covers rebuilding and normalizing surviving durations and their scalar resources. Scan contains the remaining call work, including depot checks, filters, PWL domination, theta calculation, retirement, sorting, trace work and correction bookkeeping. Stage entry and finish bookkeeping are included between their timer boundaries. Episode initialization, final counter aggregation and JSON writes are outside the measured interval. Merge maintenance uses the scan partition. Unsampled calls collect counters without reading the clock inside their episode.
+
+Loop counters cover candidate duration pieces, the sum of floored candidate demands, candidate demand-bucket counts, depot shortcuts, bucket and label visits, demand and cost breaks, actual U-subset tests and pass/reject outcomes, theta terms and subtractions, scratch functions and pieces, partial/full PWL calls and boolean outcomes, materializations, normalizations, changed costs, retirements and correction sorts. The demand statistic uses the same floor convention as bucket insertion. It is a sum, not a demand distribution. Relaxed subset checks contribute no actual subset test. A cost break counts the label whose key triggered the break.
+
+PWL counters cover completion-base calls and inspected pieces, partial early exits, pair iterations, the 4 original skip branches, actual comparisons, erase, left/right shrink and split operations. Full-only domination has separate empty/domain/gap/value exits, pair iterations, search-piece inspections and comparisons. Comparison categories are mutually exclusive. A pair containing a JUMP counts as JUMP, otherwise a pair containing CHOICE counts as CHOICE, otherwise it counts as scalar. Completion-piece inspection includes the piece that triggers the existing stopping condition. Completion counters are shared by partial/full calls within their enclosing operation, while call, pair and comparison counters remain separate.
+
+A `false` return from `DominatePieces` means some candidate survives. It can still shrink or split the scratch function. We record these mutations independently and attribute them to the final enclosing-call outcome. Mutation counts count branch executions, so a single call can shrink a prefix multiple times, including against the completion piece. No boolean result is interpreted as absence of pruning.
+
+Merge refresh counters cover input dirty buckets, deduplicated dirty buckets, visited merge entries, labels inspected, empty labels removed and stable sorts. Counts are recorded without changing retirement ownership, correction order or merge-index repair.
+
+## Local validation
+
+The standalone accounting fixture passes counter aggregation, outcome attribution, direction and operation separation, sample phase, pricing reset, exact timing partition, native status retention, unfinished handling, exclusive output and invalid-setting checks. The native PWL fixture passes 5,040 predicate and bitwise piece comparisons across both arithmetic modes, empty and point candidates, ordinary segments, CHOICE and JUMP pieces, and several domination deltas. Its OFF and ON executions produce digest `dcbfcebb1acf42ef`. Explicit mutation fixtures cover a surviving prefix shrink, a surviving interior split and full erasure.
+
+The native labeling fixture executes the selected source's existing correction invariants unchanged in both arithmetic modes and sorting settings. It additionally checks actual dominance/correction counters for U filtering, partial mutation without retirement, surviving partially pruned candidates, full-only retirement, relaxed cost skipping, merge-index repair and reset. These are synthetic native fixtures. They do not launch a routing benchmark or solve a master LP.
+
+The diagnostic `lera` static library and `_lera` bridge compile locally in the project's Nix shell with CPLEX selected. The compile commands confirm that the bridge inherits the definition and `_core` does not. The OFF equivalence fixture lexes preprocessed output, preserving whitespace inside quoted literals, and compares against a temporary archive of exact selected9d.
+
+```bash
+nix develop ./nix-dev
+cmake -S . -B build/dominance-profile-cplex -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DLERA_LP_BACKEND=cplex -DKAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILING=ON -Dpybind11_DIR="$(python -m pybind11 --cmakedir)"
+cmake --build build/dominance-profile-cplex --target _lera -j 3
+python tests/cpp/check_dominance_profile_off.py
+
+g++ -std=c++23 -O2 -DNDEBUG -ffp-contract=off -DKAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILING=1 -Icpp/lera/main/include -Icpp/lera/goc/include tests/cpp/test_dominance_profile.cpp -o build/test_dominance_profile
+build/test_dominance_profile
+
+# Compile each native fixture with the same public diagnostic definition.
+for fixture in test_dominance_profile_pwl test_dominance_profile_labeling; do
+    g++ -std=c++23 -O2 -DNDEBUG -ffp-contract=off -DKAYROS_DOMINANCE_PROFILING=1 -Icpp/lera/main/include -Icpp/lera/goc/include -Icpp/lera/nyr/include -Icpp/lera/magic_enum/include -isystem "$BOOST_INCLUDE" tests/cpp/$fixture.cpp build/dominance-profile-cplex/cpp/lera/liblera.a -L"$BOOST_BIN" -lboost_graph -ldl -lm -o build/$fixture
+    build/$fixture
+done
+```
+
+No solver trajectory, runtime advantage, or search-work equivalence has been established. Instrumentation can perturb timing and stopping points. Deterministic samples can correlate with search order, so any attribution should report sample counts and use offset repeats when needed. The original correction-off C104 measurement does not transfer to this correction-on derivative without a fresh measurement.
+
+All future routing pilots must use Dabia2013 with 25, 50 or 100 customers, CPLEX and fixed minimalLera `f2c9e20` as a control. The direct diagnostic control is uninstrumented selected9d. Retain complete source, patch, binary, input and harness hashes. Keep interrupted tasks unfinished and compare returned pools and native work signatures before interpreting timing. The active five-arm wave and selected worktree remain outside this diagnostic's scope.
